{#-
  Render a whole module when one is asked for.

  The shipped dispatch template gates its `module` branch behind
  `config.show_submodules`, but that option is not declared on the handler's
  frozen options dataclass -- setting it in `mkdocs.yml` raises "Invalid
  options", and leaving it unset makes the branch permanently false. So
  `::: @idfkit/core` collects the module successfully and then renders nothing at
  all, silently.

  Rendering by module is what keeps this reference honest: a new export appears
  on the page because it is exported, not because someone remembered to list it.
  Listing every symbol by hand instead would reintroduce exactly the drift this
  generated reference exists to remove.

  Everything that is not a module falls through to the shipped template
  untouched.
-#}
{% if obj.kind.value == "module" %}
  {% with module = obj %}
    {% include "module.html.jinja" with context %}
  {% endwith %}
{% else %}
  {% include "_base/dispatch.html.jinja" with context %}
{% endif %}
